```

When `chr == '$' && peek(lexer) == '{'`:
1. `chr = next(lexer)` reads `$`, `pos` advances.
2. `peek(lexer)` calls `next()` (reads `{`, `pos` advances), then `backup()` (pos-- back to after `$`).
3. `peek(lexer) == '{'` is true.
4. `backup(lexer)`: `pos--`. Now `pos` points to `$`.
5. `emit(lexer, LEXEME_STRING)`: sets `start = pos` (at `$`).
6. `advance_n(lexer, strlen("{"))`: `pos += 1` (past `{`), `start = pos`.

This is fine. But what if `$` is at position `start` (the very beginning of the token being lexed)?

